# Project Copy

Follow `@.cursor/rules/soul.mdc` and use the writer skill.

## Description

- Describe what the project is and does, not Gabo's contribution.
- Use one or two short sentences and stay near 160 characters when possible.
- Keep the description useful as metadata and a standalone masonry card.
- Put ownership and implementation detail in `role`, `achievements`, and `story`.
- Avoid pitch-deck framing, fundraising, TAM, and parent-company audience claims unless they are essential project facts.

## Facts

- Package markdown owns project technology, architecture, achievements, links, and year.
- The website CV owns employment title and duration.
- Use `role` only when the CV verifies it.
- Keep `featured` only for `legal-agent`, `wink`, `ztx`, `bitlauncher`, `opyn`, and `eos-costa-rica`.
- Do not add `tier` or `outcome` fields.

Never invent users, reactions, quotes, dates, metrics, titles, or anecdotes. Preserve valid achievements, technology tags, story details, and links when compressing.
